cribed it to me this way  he said that the most revealing  interview he saw was a lifelong democrat  asking why he's voting for Donald Trump  and this blue-collar guy said because my  country's got kima on my country's got  cancer and Donald Trump's just the  chemotherapy we need hard to disqualify  chemotherapy by simply calling it  poisoned repeatedly what people are  looking for and what Hillary Clinton has  to offer are the actions that we can  take together that will complete this  story of America's recovery in such a  way that not only is our country doing  better by creating more jobs but  families are doing better by creating  more income we need to make wages go up  and not down and and that's I believe  the task before Hillary Clinton in this  next debate we certainly had a lot of  people in our primaries that also just  wanted to break the kitchen table but  breaking the kitchen table doesn't put  food on it is that a reference to Bernie  Sanders I mean is that certainly the the  dynamic of the Sanders campaign was yes  damn right people should be angry is  that what sort of you're referring to  yes I am and I think it was as Donald  Trump's as Donald Trump's appeal was  also complicated by racial fears and  fear of the world xenophobia I think  that part of the appeal on the left and  our party was also fueled by Donald  Trump's rise by our failure to debate  him from or to take the debate stage  ourselves as Democrats from June through  October as heroes and a lot of people in  our party but well if we're not going to  have a more contested primary the only  thing left to do is is to protest both  the both the front-running candidate and  also the rise of Donald Trump I think  Bernie Sanders made some really good  points in the primary  they were point that he's been making  for 40 years about income inequality and  he really had that message honed to to a  fine fine tune  this platform has primary Hillary  Clinton took the best ideas the Bernie  Sanders in the fight for on affordable  college but the platform also  incorporates something I advanced  traffic and clean energy grid by 2050 -  the United States of America for the  first time we are advocating in our  party's platform repeal of the death  penalty so our party's contest was one  of ideas and in this year of anger and  protests the ideas what we well we  talked about them analyst the the you  know the hallmark of I think this year  will be people's profound desire to  protest all right we've been speaking  with former Maryland governor and former  2016 Democratic presidential candidate  martin O'Malley thanks so much for  joining us we will take a break and be  back with more right after this

